WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.879
Star Wars: The Last Jedi has arrived at last,
leaving audiences thrilled, amazed, and emotionally

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:10.680
spent — not to mention totally wondering
exactly what the heck is going to happen next.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.940
Unfortunately, that "next" isn't going to
arrive until Episode IX hits theaters in 2019,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.640
but at least that gives fans plenty of time
to speculate about just what we're likely

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.570
to see when this story finally concludes.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.360
With that in mind, here's a spoiler-filled
look at some of the biggest unanswered questions

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.400
in The Last Jedi.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.980
Why did Luke die?

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.400
Just as it seemed all hope was lost for the
Resistance at the end of The Last Jedi, the

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.899
actual last Jedi showed up with a new hope
in the form of a cool Force projection from

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:39.329
across the galaxy.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:43.670
And then, after giving the others time to
escape, he dropped dead...for no apparent

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.670
reason.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.670
But why?

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.239
Was the strain of projecting himself across
the galaxy too much?

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.550
Did Kylo Ren's lightsaber attacks somehow
actually injure Luke in the same way Kylo

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.219
was able to reach out and physically touch
Rey from across the galaxy?

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:00.410
Or did Luke simply become one with the Force
after redeeming himself and finally finding

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.410
balance?

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.120
All we know for sure is, like Yoda before
him, Luke just suddenly raptured on out of

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.969
there, leaving behind nothing but a sweaty
old Jedi snuggie.

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:10.110
Why, though, is anyone's guess.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.479
Were Snoke's guards actually Luke's other
students?

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:17.670
When Luke explains to Rey what happened between
him and Kylo Ren, he states that Ben Solo

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.951
turned to the Dark Side, slew several of Luke's
other students, and then took off with the

00:01:21.951 --> 00:01:22.951
rest.

00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:24.840
So what happened to those other students?

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.700
Is it possible they ended up as Snoke's personal
guards?

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.250
After all, those mysterious red clad warriors
were almost powerful enough to take out Kylo

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.969
Ren and Rey at the same time.

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:38.070
Of course, if those were Luke's other students,
why wasn't anybody looking for them and trying

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.820
to save them instead of only worrying about
Kylo Ren all the time?

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.200
And if they weren't Luke's other students,
does that mean some of Luke's other students

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.030
might still be alive somewhere?

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.030
Hmm...

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.149
Is Snoke really dead?

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:53.609
There was a ton of speculation over the last
couple years over Supreme Leader Snoke's true

00:01:53.609 --> 00:01:54.609
identity.

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:58.640
And then he abruptly got cut in half with
a lightsaber, making all that speculation

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.640
pointless.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.640
Whoops!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.689
But is he really dead?

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:05.619
One of the leading theories about Snoke's
true identity was the idea that he was actually

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:11.420
Darth Plagueis, a Sith Lord who was so incredibly
powerful, he actually mastered death itself.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.940
If that's true, then it's possible Snoke could
possibly return from the dead in Episode IX.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.280
And hey, Darth Maul somehow came back from
being cut in half by grafting weird spider

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.500
legs to his torso.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.220
So is the galaxy going to be menaced by Zombie
Snoke?

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.550
Let the next two years of speculation begin.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.030
What are they going to do with Leia?

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.420
When Carrie Fisher tragically passed away
in 2016, fans couldn't help but wonder how

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.360
it would affect the Star Wars universe.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.390
While Fisher had already finished filming
her scenes as General Leia for The Last Jedi,

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.590
Disney reportedly had to completely rework
the story for Episode IX to deal with the

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.650
loss of one of the franchise's most beloved
characters.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.150
But how exactly are they going to handle it
in the story?

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:53.670
At the end of The Last Jedi, Leia is still
leading the ragtag group of survivors from

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.950
the Resistance, and is confident she has all
the tools she needs to reform the movement

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.810
and drive out the First Order.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:04.590
But since Disney is reportedly not going to
use any footage of Fisher in Episode IX, or

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:09.110
use CGI to recreate her as they did in Rogue
One, it leaves a major question mark about

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.340
how they'll explain her absence.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.400
Why is Luke really on the island?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.860
When Rey shows up and asks for Luke's help,
he very rudely tells her to get lost, informing

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.040
her that he came to the island to die in peace.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.200
Which is a nice line and everything, but it
doesn't make a lick of sense.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.260
For starters, if he wanted to die, why is
he... still, like, alive?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.280
And more importantly: if he really wanted
to be alone so darn badly, why did he leave

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.470
behind a detailed map showing exactly how
to find him?

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:38.640
The whole thing seems like the Jedi equivalent
of vaguebooking: he really went away because

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.530
he just wanted someone to come find him and
ask what's wrong.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.880
And you thought Kylo Ren was the emo one.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.210
What's in the cave?

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.060
Jedi trainees sure do love going into evil
caves to confront the Dark Side.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.980
But Rey's trip into the blowhole of ultimate
evil left us with more questions than answers.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.610
When she first senses the cave, Luke is horrified
at how willingly she approaches the darkness

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.980
that dwells within.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:05.030
but not horrified enough to cancel the next
lesson...They agree that there must be something

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.120
Rey needs inside the cave, something that
calls to her.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:12.120
And yet, when she actually goes inside to
find out what the deal is, she only finds

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.070
a mirror that provides her with… nothing
at all.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.160
So what was Rey drawn to in the cave that
was so important?

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.070
Because whatever it is, she didn't seem to
actually find it.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.430
What are Leia's powers?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.430
Fans have been salivating at the idea of Leia
becoming a Jedi knight since it was first

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:32.010
revealed in Return of the Jedi that she's
Luke's sister and can also use the Force.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:36.290
But other than occasionally gazing into the
middle distance and mumbling someone's name,

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.250
she never seemed to use any of her powers
— until The Last Jedi, when she suddenly

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.910
went full on star wizard in a crazy sequence
when she used her abilities to survive the

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.620
vacuum of space and even fly through it.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.430
Which begs the question: how the heck did
she do that?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.780
When did she undergo training?

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.780
What else can she do?

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.650
Leia's powers have never been explored, but
flying around in space like you're Iron Man

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.740
or something suggests that Leia has a whole
bag of tricks we never knew about — and,

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.070
sadly, are never likely to see again.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.810
What does porg taste like?

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.139
It's true that Last Jedi leaves a lot of questions
open to debate.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:13.220
But for our money, the one question we really
want answered is what porg tastes like.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.620
In one of the most wrenching scenes in the
film, Chewbacca tries to eat a roast porg,

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.590
only to be accosted by the poor beast's distraught
family.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.260
They try to guilt him into not eating their
cousin, although by that point, the damage

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.540
was kind of already done.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.490
And it looked delicious, like a juicy, tender
chicken roasted to perfection.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.490
But does it taste like chicken?

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.270
Or, as the name implies, is it closer to pork?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.240
Porg: the other, other white meat?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.720
It does kind of have a ring to it.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.720
Thanks for watching!

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.310
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.590
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

